concept tables {
  name     = "Tables"
  summary  = "Pipe-row syntax for writing many records of the same shape compactly."
  related  = [lists, records]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "Repeated rows of the same shape can be written with pipe-table syntax under a field name. Each `| ... |` row becomes one record."
    h2 "Authoring"
    p "The field's row type carries a `@table(\"kind\")` decorator. The field declaration uses `name:` (colon, not `=`) and lists rows directly underneath."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
@table("user")
type User {
  name:    utf8
  age:     u32
  enabled: bool
}

@document
type Config {
  users: list<User>
}

users:
  | "alice" | 30 | true  |
  | "bob"   | 25 | false |
  | "cara"  | 42 | true  |
SRC
    }
    h2 "Why a table"
    p "A table is just a `list<T>` underneath — the pipe-row syntax is shorthand for writing many [records](concept_records) compactly. The same data could be authored as block instances, but the table is denser and reads like a spreadsheet."
    callout "Cells are expressions" { class = ["info"]  body = "Each cell is an expression in the row type's field position: strings, numbers, booleans, symbols, even computed values via let bindings." }
  }
}
